{
  "case_id": "2022-21-1239",
  "document_hash": "a671525d0a48bf130c50cedae36f835bc046558cbeac2b2c5b0f02bb69d0ba33",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Michelle Cochran",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a671525d0a48bf130c50cedae36f835bc046558cbeac2b2c5b0f02bb69d0ba33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a671525d0a48-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question in this companion case is whether the SEC Act strips district courts of jurisdiction that they have historically possessed to adjudicate and enjoin structural constitutional violations, here, in the form of an agency decision-maker that is unconstitutionally insulated from removal by the President."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a671525d0a48bf130c50cedae36f835bc046558cbeac2b2c5b0f02bb69d0ba33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a671525d0a48-0000-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We'll hear argument next in Case 21-1239, SEC versus Cochran."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a671525d0a48bf130c50cedae36f835bc046558cbeac2b2c5b0f02bb69d0ba33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a671525d0a48-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Can -- can I take you back to Free Enterprise Fund following along Justice Kavanaugh's question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a671525d0a48bf130c50cedae36f835bc046558cbeac2b2c5b0f02bb69d0ba33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a671525d0a48-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I still don't understand. Is there something special about structural constitutional claims?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a671525d0a48bf130c50cedae36f835bc046558cbeac2b2c5b0f02bb69d0ba33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a671525d0a48-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GARRE: So I think this Court has recognized that structural constitutional claims are different in terms of how they inflict injury that's separate and unique."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Garre",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a671525d0a48bf130c50cedae36f835bc046558cbeac2b2c5b0f02bb69d0ba33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a671525d0a48-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GARRE: So the APA non-jurisdictional arguments are waived in our case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a671525d0a48bf130c50cedae36f835bc046558cbeac2b2c5b0f02bb69d0ba33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a671525d0a48-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the Court said the same thing in Standard Oil, that it didn't expect the agency to devote any more resources to the reason to believe determination."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a671525d0a48bf130c50cedae36f835bc046558cbeac2b2c5b0f02bb69d0ba33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a671525d0a48-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Can I ask you about your reliance on collateral order doctrine cases? It's not clear to me why the situation here is in any meaningful sense parallel to the situation in a case where a party invokes the collateral order doctrine."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a671525d0a48bf130c50cedae36f835bc046558cbeac2b2c5b0f02bb69d0ba33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a671525d0a48-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the statutory language pushes in the opposite direction because 1331, if you just read it literally, gives the district court jurisdiction over that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a671525d0a48bf130c50cedae36f835bc046558cbeac2b2c5b0f02bb69d0ba33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a671525d0a48-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Is the APA argument waivable?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1239",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a671525d0a48bf130c50cedae36f835bc046558cbeac2b2c5b0f02bb69d0ba33",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a671525d0a48-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Yes, one question. On Justice Gorsuch's questions, how relevant is 703, which is the provision -- you referenced it earlier -- that says \"the form of proceeding for judicial review is the special statutory review proceeding relevant to the subject matter in a court.\" Is that relevant at all?"
    },
